HST Office: more of Word's VBA object model in HST Writer (owner request for 1.0.0-beta.5).

- Document.InlineShapes (new XInlineShape/XInlineShapes, sw/source/ui/vba/vbainlineshapes.*):
  Count, Item, For Each, AddPicture(FileName, LinkToFile, SaveWithDocument, Range) inserting the
  picture as character at its natural size; InlineShape.Width/Height (points), LockAspectRatio
  (keeps the proportions when one side changes), Type, Range, Delete, Select.
- Document.Comments (new XComment/XComments, sw/source/ui/vba/vbacomments.*): Count, Item,
  For Each, Add(Range, Text) spanning the range, with the user's name as author; Comment.Range
  (the comment text), Scope (the commented text), Author, Initial, Delete.
- Fields.Add for PAGE, NUMPAGES, DATE and TIME (by WdFieldType or field code); Fields.Update also
  updates the tables of contents and other indexes, as in Word.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); the new files are
MPL-2.0 like their neighbours.
Test: tests/runtime/check-vba.py (writer-inlineshapes*, writer-comments, writer-fields*).
